<%- include('partials/head') %>
<div class="pagehead"><div>
  <span class="label">For North Carolina contractors and homeowners</span>
  <h1>The homeowner pays the whole job up front. The contractor is paid step by step as the work passes inspection.</h1>
</div></div>
<div class="grid2">
  <div class="card stack"><h2>For contractors</h2>
    <p>Offer the plan to your homeowner. They deposit the full job price before you start, so you know the money is there. Each time a step passes an independent inspection or a permit inspection, you're paid by instant transfer.</p>
    <p><a class="btn primary" href="/signup">Create a contractor account</a></p></div>
  <div class="card stack"><h2>For homeowners</h2>
    <p>Your money is held by Stripe, a licensed payment company, and released only when an inspector who works for neither side, or the permit office, confirms the work is done. If something goes wrong, the step on hold stays frozen until it's resolved.</p>
    <p class="muted small">Homeowners join through the invite link their contractor sends.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="card stack"><h2>How a job works</h2>
  <ol class="stack" style="margin:0;padding-left:1.2rem">
    <li>The contractor sets up the job, the payment steps and the estimated permit fees, then invites the homeowner.</li>
    <li>The homeowner accepts and deposits the job price, the permit fee fund, and a 1.25% service fee.</li>
    <li>The contractor finishes a step and uploads photos. An independent inspector visits, or the permit office inspects.</li>
    <li>When the step passes, the contractor is paid that step's amount less a 1.25% service fee.</li>
    <li>Any permit money left at the end goes back to the homeowner.</li>
  </ol></div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
